Z||000000||Hank is Here||09-27-2001||05:18 PM||||Okay I saw this on a convertabe this summer when I was visiting cliff. <BR>The subframe seems to be made out of 1 inch box tubing (that metric inches not standard :bs <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  This is all I have so please don't ask me for any more info pics, hopefully this will help someone out.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7070011.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7070011.jpg"> <P>I appoligize to the Fiero shop in the NL if they did not want these pics to get out. I figure that most of us are across the ocean and are not taking away from their business.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||09-27-2001||06:23 PM||||When i was reinforcing mine, i used 2" x 1/4" square stock.  The 1" i could flex by hand when it was in 5 foot lengths.  Drawback however is lowering the car would make speedbumps and railroad tracks even more hazardous, but there isn't the slightest amount of flex  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
